    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] 2026-11-01 review at dev 100b6fbb6e: fixture interface Shape; enum Kind implements Shape; record Circle implements Shape; class Sq implements Shape. survey emits implements for Sq and Circle (plus dispatches_to Shape.area -> Sq.area / Circle.area) and nothing for Kind or Kind.area. The guard is now java.py L2767 (root_cause cites ~L2547); gikuk 495f9747f5 changed how the extends source is found but not which node types are handled. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFound by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit and reproduced on the shipped CLI: for 'enum Kind implements Shape' no implements edge exists, while 'record Circle(...) implements Shape' (inheritance-linker) and 'class Sq implements Shape' (java) both have one. Consequence: enum method dispatch through the interface is invisible to inherited_calls and type_hierarchy. java.py's module docstring now states the gap."  # e554
